SUMMARY:Econometrics – Andres Ramirez Hassan (Universidad EAFIT) – Exte
 rnal Validity as Prediction: Hierarchical Modeling of Treatment Effect Het
 erogeneity
LOCATION:Room 404\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Andres Ramirez Hassan: “External Validity as Prediction: Hier
 archical Modeling of Treatment Effect Heterogeneity”\nhttps://sites.goog
 le.com/view/arh-bayesian\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/85966225829?pw
 d=g6hOdHyvYB0qta0aFzGbWOgczJ1Qzr.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl
 /BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nWe develop a hierarchical framework for e
 xternal validity in settings with heterogeneous treatment effects and indi
 vidual-level microdata. We recast external validity as a prediction proble
 m: the object of interest is the treatment effect in a new target setting\
 , whose predictability is governed by cross-study and individual-level het
 erogeneity. The model decomposes treatment-effect variation into systemati
 c components explained by observed individual- and study-level characteris
 tics and residual cross-study heterogeneity that limits generalization\, a
 nd quantifies external validity through the posterior predictive distribut
 ion in new settings. We establish large-sample properties under fixed-stud
 y and many-studies asymptotics: predictive uncertainty does not vanish---w
 hether within-study samples grow large or the number of studies grows---un
 less residual cross-study heterogeneity is zero. The framework nests stand
 ard meta-analysis as a special case. Applied to the Project STAR experimen
 t\, the framework reveals substantial individual-level heterogeneity with 
 limited systematic explanation from observed school characteristics\, and 
 hence persistent predictive uncertainty when extrapolating to new settings
 .
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/85966225829?pwd=g6hOdHyvYB0qta0aFzGbWOgczJ1Qz
 r.1
END:VEVENT
